# Ground truth for looped-phrase.wav. Derived from independent oracles, NOT from
# bass2tably's own output.
#
# The take is one 15-note phrase played four times, exactly 8.0 s apart.
# Every note below is backed by an onset from `aubioonset -B 2048 -H 256`
# and a stable pitch from `aubiopitch -p yin -B 4096 -H 1024`. Folding the
# oracle onsets over the 8.0 s period lands all four repetitions on the same
# phases, so each note is confirmed four times over.
#
# Do NOT regenerate this file from bass2tably's output. A previous version was
# blessed that way and locked in a false negative: the A1 at 5.03 s of every
# repetition (55.8 Hz, confirmed by both oracles) was recorded as absent, so
# the suite stayed green while the pipeline dropped four real notes.
#
# Two notes per repetition were recovered after this file was first written from
# ground truth: the A1 at 5.03 s (the pitch stage rejected it) and the F#1 at
# 2.57 s (the onset stage did not see it). Both were predicted from the oracles
# before the code changed, and both landed at the predicted times.
#
# This list is what the pipeline should currently find, not necessarily
# everything that is played. The oracles also show same-pitch repeats that could
# not be told apart from onset re-triggers by signal alone. See "Known
# limitations" in README.md.

28 30 33 30 28 28 30 30 28 30 33 30 28 28 35 36
28 30 33 30 28 28 30 30 28 30 33 30 28 28 35 36
28 30 33 30 28 28 30 30 28 30 33 30 28 28 35 36
28 30 33 30 28 28 30 30 28 30 33 30 28 28 35 36
